What are Microservices?

Microservices is an architectural style where an application is divided into multiple small, independent services. Each service performs a specific business function and communicates with other services using REST APIs.

Advantages
Independent deployment
Easy maintenance
Better scalability
Fault isolation
Faster development by different teams
ACCOUNT MICROSERVICE
1. pom.xml

The pom.xml file manages all dependencies required for the Account Service.

Dependencies
spring-boot-starter-web
Used to create REST APIs.
spring-boot-devtools
Automatically restarts the application during development.
spring-boot-starter-test
Provides JUnit and testing libraries.
2. Account Model

The Account class is a Java Bean that stores account information.

