Monolithic vs Microservices
Monolithic Architecture	Microservices Architecture
Single application	Multiple independent services
Single deployment	Independent deployment
Difficult to scale	Easy to scale each service
Single point of failure	Failure of one service doesn't affect others
Entire application must be redeployed	Only modified service needs deployment
One technology stack	Different technologies can be used
Benefits of Microservices
1. Independent Services

Each microservice works separately without depending on others.

2. Different Ports
Account Service → 8080
Loan Service → 8081
3. Fault Isolation

If one service crashes, the other services continue running.

4. Team Collaboration

Different teams can develop different services simultaneously.

5. Independent Deployment

Each service can be updated and deployed without affecting other services.
